diff --git a/docs/runbooks/lab-promotion.md b/docs/runbooks/lab-promotion.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000..a82f5ee55c
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/runbooks/lab-promotion.md
@@ -0,0 +1,114 @@
+# Lab Promotion Runbook
+
+Operator runbook for promoting a lab app out of `apps/labs/*` into its durable
+lawful home (D10: v1 is a documented process — there is no `beep labs promote`
+command). Doctrine lives in
+[`standards/architecture/14-lab-apps.md`](../../standards/architecture/14-lab-apps.md);
+this file is the step list. The common case promotes a whole lab into a
+production app at `apps/<name>`; step 9 covers the other homes.
+
+Everything below lands in **one PR**: the move, full registration and ceremony
+onboarding, consumer migration, and removal of every residual lab surface.
+
+## 1. Flip the disposition first
+
+Edit `apps/labs/<name>/lab.manifest.json` and set
+`"disposition": "promote"`. This records operator intent before the move; it
+may land with the lab's last change or at the start of the promotion PR.
+
+## 2. Choose the smallest lawful durable home
+
+An app under `apps/`, the owning slice, a shared-kernel promotion, a driver,
+a foundation package, a tooling package, or an ecosystem package. A promotion
+that creates or changes a shared export follows that home's admission and
+decision-record requirements — lab status never waives them. The rest of this
+runbook assumes the `apps/<name>` case.
+
+## 3. Move the tree
+
+```sh
+git mv apps/labs/<name> apps/<name>
+```
+
+No root workspace edit is needed: the root `package.json` `"apps/*"` glob
+already covers the new path, and the `"apps/labs/*"` glob simply stops
+matching.
+
+## 4. Delete the lab entry
+
+- `git rm apps/<name>/lab.manifest.json` — promoted apps carry no lab
+  manifest.
+- Remove the lab notice line from the app's `AGENTS.md`.
+
+## 5. Rename the portless hostname
+
+Labs serve at `<name>.labs.beep.localhost:1355`; production apps at
+`<name>.beep.localhost:1355`. Update:
+
+- the `dev` script in `apps/<name>/package.json`:
+  `portless <name>.labs.beep …` → `portless <name>.beep …`;
+- any `allowedDevOrigins` entry in `next.config.ts` (nextjs kind);
+- the URL in the app's `README.md`.
+
+## 6. Recompute relative hops
+
+The tree is now one directory level shallower. Fix every path that hopped out
+of `apps/labs/<name>`:
+
+- `tsconfig.json` `extends`: `../../../tsconfig.base.json` (was
+  `../../../../`);
+- `vitest.config.ts` shared-config import: `../../vitest.shared.ts`-style hops
+  drop one `../`;
+- any other `../../../../` reference emitted by the lab template.
+
+## 7. Full registration and ceremony onboarding
+
+Labs are ceremony-exempt by path; at `apps/<name>` the exemption ends. Add:
+
+- **Docgen**: an `apps/<name>/docgen.json` (model:
+  `apps/practice-kg-mcp/docgen.json`; fix `$schema` hops and `srcLink`) plus a
+  `"docgen": "bun run ../../packages/tooling/tool/docgen/src/bin.ts"` script.
+  Prove with `bun run docgen:local`.
+- **Coverage**: a `"coverage": "bunx vitest run --coverage"` script (matches
+  `apps/oip-web/package.json`).
+- **Root TS references**: run `bun run beep tsconfig-sync` — the labs
+  exclusion no longer applies, so the app re-enters `tsconfig.packages.json`.
+  Prove with `bun run beep tsconfig-sync --check`.
+- **Changesets**: the package now participates. Author a changeset for the
+  promotion (`bunx changeset`) and prove with
+  `bun run beep quality changeset-status` — the labs-path exemption must no
+  longer be what makes it pass.
+
+## 8. Move the identity composer (identity is KEPT)
+
+In `packages/foundation/modeling/identity/src/packages.ts`, move the app's
+composer entry out of the `generatedLabComposers` region (fenced by
+`// GENERATED LAB EXPORTS START` / `// GENERATED LAB EXPORTS END`) into the
+authored `generatedComposers` package group. Keep the same accessor
+(`$<PascalName>Id`) — promotion preserves package identity unless semantic
+ownership actually changed, in which case record an explicit identity
+transition. If this was the last lab, remove the fenced region entirely: the
+generated labs region is absent in the zero-lab state.
+
+## 9. Promotion into a non-app home
+
+When the durable home is a package, mint it with the factory
+(`bun run beep create-package …` or `bun run beep architecture` for slice
+files), move the earned code in, migrate all consumers in the same PR, then
+delete the remaining lab shell:
+
+```sh
+bun run beep delete-package @beep/<name>
+```
+
+If the lab's manifest declared a `postgresSchema`, the delete drops it only
+with the explicit `--drop-data` consent flag; without consent it prints the
+manual drop steps and leaves data intact.
+
+## 10. Verify clean
+
+- `rg -n "labs/<name>"` — hits only in historical records
+  (`goals/`, `research/`, changelogs), never in live config or code;
+- `bun run beep tsconfig-sync --check` and
+  `bun run beep quality changeset-status` pass;
+- `bun run beep yeet verify` green before publish.
